  /// provide this value, GuardDuty verifies that the specified account owns
  /// the bucket before it exports findings. If the account ID doesn't match
  /// the actual owner of the bucket, GuardDuty doesn't export findings to
  /// that bucket. This helps prevent GuardDuty from exporting your findings
  /// to a bucket that a different Amazon Web Services account owns (for
  /// example, if the original bucket was deleted and its name was later
  /// claimed by another account). If you don't specify this value, GuardDuty
  /// doesn't perform this verification. GuardDuty strongly recommends that
  /// you provide the expected bucket owner when possible. When you update a
  /// publishing destination, omitting this field leaves the currently stored
  /// value unchanged. This field appears in the response only if it was
  /// provided when the publishing destination was created or updated. For
